{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#452","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#452","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#452\",\"parent_revision\":\"a89c821490e0da4c97610a6610088b6d134b2632\",\"root_revision\":\"71f0ca246e16fd624c8a8428fc4cdcd3a614067df64f4f458c87b6d3d719489a\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nimplement-feature dispatches all ready tasks in parallel with no upper bound. A task plan with 20 ready P1 tasks would spawn 20 concurrent agents simultaneously, exhausting API rate limits and making logs unreadable.\\n\\nSymphony enforces: `available_slots = max(max_concurrent_agents - running_count, 0)`. Both the global cap and per-state caps can be changed in WORKFLOW.md and take effect at runtime.\\n\\n**Proposed behaviour:**\\n- Add `max_concurrent_tasks` setting (default: 5) readable from task file frontmatter or a `plan/config.yaml`.\\n- implement-feature skill: before dispatching wave N, count currently IN PROGRESS tasks (via `implementation_manager.py status`); dispatch only `max_concurrent_tasks - in_progress_count` tasks in the next wave.\\n- Optional: per-priority cap (e.g., max 2 P1 tasks at once, unlimited P2).\\n- Wave loop: after each wave completes, re-query ready tasks and dispatch the next batch within the cap.\\n\\n**Acceptance criteria:**\\n- With 10 ready tasks and cap=5, implement-feature dispatches 5, waits for completions, then dispatches remaining 5.\\n- Cap of 0 or negative is rejected with a clear error.\\n- Setting is optional; omitting it defaults to current unlimited behaviour for backwards compatibility.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Snapshot: Concurrency cap for parallel task dispatch in implement-feature\\nDate: 2026-04-23\\nGoal: Add max_concurrent_tasks setting and wave dispatch logic to implement-feature.\\n\\nConditions:\\n1. implement-feature dispatch loop | AVAILABLE | plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md Progress Loop section\\n2. in-progress task count query | AVAILABLE | via sam_plan(action='status') \u2014 by_status counts available\\n3. max_concurrent_tasks setting location | DERIVABLE | task file frontmatter or plan/config.yaml; default 5\\n4. Per-priority cap option | DERIVABLE | optional feature; default is total cap\\n\\nAVAILABLE count: 2\\nDERIVABLE count: 2\\nMISSING count: 0\\n\\nDecision: APPROVED \u2014 wave dispatch logic is clear; setting location is the main design decision.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **concurrency cap for parallel task dispatch in implement-feature** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: OpenAI Symphony SPEC.md \u00a75.3 \u2014 global max_concurrent_agents (default 10) and optional per-state caps; available slots = max(max_concurrent_agents - running_count, 0)\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-06\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-23)\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- [ ] `implement-feature` SKILL.md Progress Loop reads `max_concurrent_tasks` from plan config (default 5 when absent)\\n- [ ] Before dispatching wave N, orchestrator counts `in_progress` tasks via `sam_plan(action='status')` and dispatches at most `max_concurrent_tasks - in_progress_count` new tasks\\n- [ ] With 10 ready tasks and cap=5: first wave dispatches 5, waits for completions, second wave dispatches remaining 5\\n- [ ] Cap=0 or negative produces a clear error before any dispatch\\n- [ ] Omitting the cap setting defaults to current unlimited behavior (backwards compatible)\\n- [ ] `uv run prek run --files plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` passes\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` \u2014 Progress Loop (add cap check)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py` \u2014 Plan model (add max_concurrent_tasks field, optional)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/` \u2014 document max_concurrent_tasks in config or TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs an **implement-feature orchestrator dispatching tasks in parallel**, I want **a configurable `max_concurrent_tasks` cap** so that **I don't spawn 20 simultaneous agents and exhaust API rate limits on large plans**.\\n\",\"digest\":\"18734f39462611b8b72de32569ae5c5086b5dd6d9ee5428be11d406faab22fcb\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPg0yfA\"}"}